WEBVTT

00:01.870 --> 00:06.760
<i>My guess is that it was 
one of the undergrounders.</i>

00:06.760 --> 00:08.630
<i>You mean the waste tower?</i>

00:10.090 --> 00:14.450
Well, students, this is the gathering 
area in the waste tower.

01:59.900 --> 02:02.050
Let's begin, then.

02:06.070 --> 02:08.450
There are plants and gems

02:08.450 --> 02:12.930
that can only be found at the ends of 
ancient summers, on the night of Hallowe'en.

02:14.500 --> 02:17.360
But, there's a condition you need to satisfy.

02:20.480 --> 02:21.410
Here.

02:21.410 --> 02:22.040
See this?

02:25.810 --> 02:27.010
No.

02:28.340 --> 02:29.680
Okay.

02:29.680 --> 02:30.960
You two.

02:30.960 --> 02:32.120
Yes.

02:32.120 --> 02:34.210
You two look for the minerals.

02:35.030 --> 02:38.630
Sergeant, teach them how to gather these.

02:39.240 --> 02:39.960
Yes, sir.

02:40.240 --> 02:42.920
Meet back here in thirty minutes.

02:44.630 --> 02:47.550
To think there are two of 
them that are qualified...

02:48.210 --> 02:49.930
Minerals team!

02:49.930 --> 02:51.200
Coming!

02:52.930 --> 02:55.860
What is that?

02:56.570 --> 02:57.710
Dunno.

02:58.520 --> 03:01.170
Look for those.

03:01.780 --> 03:05.430
Grab them by the petals and 
cut them above the root.

03:06.310 --> 03:08.700
What's the condition that 
lets you see those things?

03:11.340 --> 03:14.680
I think you're better off not knowing.

03:15.760 --> 03:17.640
Speak more clearly!

03:19.930 --> 03:21.600
Let's go, Philomela.

03:25.670 --> 03:29.910
<i>Rian's weirdly aggressive towards Philomela.</i>

03:36.430 --> 03:38.240
Trick or treat?

03:39.020 --> 03:40.290
Trick.

03:48.090 --> 03:50.690
That's a nasty trick.

03:53.010 --> 03:56.450
I've grown up enough to 
knock you onto the floor now.

03:57.560 --> 03:58.820
You're right.

03:59.300 --> 04:00.990
You've certainly grown up.

04:00.990 --> 04:04.510
But that would have been 
nothing if you had your arm.

04:05.290 --> 04:08.010
You don't need to worry about this.

04:08.410 --> 04:12.190
Like I said before, you don't 
need to protect me, either.

04:13.050 --> 04:14.780
You're a child. Do as you like.

04:15.020 --> 04:19.080
Isn't it part of a parent's job 
to support their kid's dreams?!

04:19.910 --> 04:21.230
Jeez...

04:22.170 --> 04:25.230
I'd hoped to give you a goal that you 
could work towards for a while.

04:25.830 --> 04:27.750
I never thought you'd get so obsessed.

04:30.950 --> 04:33.040
How is it any different 
from a kid who wants

04:33.040 --> 04:34.910
to be a firefighter
 actually becoming one?

04:35.430 --> 04:36.870
It happens all the time.

04:39.480 --> 04:43.250
Do you hate it that much when 
I treat you like my daughter?

04:51.520 --> 04:52.650
Zoe?

04:53.400 --> 04:54.380
Chise.

04:54.940 --> 04:55.860
Are you all right?

04:55.860 --> 04:56.930
Yeah.

04:57.450 --> 05:00.410
This place is scary, though.

05:00.740 --> 05:04.090
I feel like I'm being watched.

05:04.090 --> 05:06.900
Not by faeries or spirits, though.

05:08.460 --> 05:10.240
I think you're right.

05:10.680 --> 05:14.020
It's not just living things, 
but also dead things.

05:14.020 --> 05:16.530
Is that because it's Hallowe'en?

05:16.530 --> 05:17.690
I don't know.

05:17.690 --> 05:19.120
Still, be careful.

05:19.120 --> 05:21.490
You probably shouldn't be on your own.

05:22.690 --> 05:23.570
Yeah.

05:23.570 --> 05:25.790
We have to gather stuff, too, though.

05:25.790 --> 05:26.900
Yeah...

05:32.070 --> 05:32.910
Found one.

05:43.340 --> 05:45.330
Torch, burn the wicked being.

05:50.500 --> 05:53.570
That's a beast that uses 
the form of a flower as bait.

05:55.920 --> 05:57.760
You've always been so skilled.

05:57.760 --> 05:59.580
It's true now, just as much as before.

06:00.010 --> 06:01.340
So what's your problem?

06:02.550 --> 06:06.160
I'm not good enough for my grandmother.

06:06.490 --> 06:08.720
I'm asking about what <i>you</i> want!

06:10.260 --> 06:12.320
You'd never understand.

06:13.530 --> 06:15.850
Especially if you don't <i>tell</i> me!

06:20.830 --> 06:23.010
That's the thing about you.

06:25.360 --> 06:28.030
My dad was a piece of shit.

06:29.630 --> 06:31.440
You're not like him.

06:32.830 --> 06:38.480
Regardless, if you're ever in grave 
danger, I'll continue stepping up.

06:38.480 --> 06:39.670
But why?!

06:40.490 --> 06:44.030
Because I was protected like that as well.

06:44.690 --> 06:46.420
By my father.

06:46.700 --> 06:49.290
Like how, though?

06:52.740 --> 06:56.340
If it bothers you,
I'll start getting involved.

06:56.340 --> 06:59.070
Seriously, what does that even mean?!

06:59.830 --> 07:00.930
Don't run off!

07:01.770 --> 07:04.910
Even I have things that 
I don't like talking about.

07:04.910 --> 07:06.150
Hey!

07:06.150 --> 07:08.340
You haven't been eating 
much lately, have you?!

07:08.340 --> 07:10.550
You've got such a wussy face!

07:10.550 --> 07:11.970
You'd better eat!

07:12.430 --> 07:13.450
As should you.

07:13.800 --> 07:17.120
I hope you aren't still a fussy 
eater when I'm not watching.

07:17.120 --> 07:18.750
I'm not!

07:20.480 --> 07:25.010
<i>I'm still not getting anywhere.</i>

07:26.090 --> 07:27.910
That's just fine.

07:28.370 --> 07:31.460
There are some things only kids can do.

07:32.790 --> 07:36.100
What did he mean, he was protected?

07:36.340 --> 07:37.690
Who knows?

07:38.750 --> 07:41.220
Do you think Adolf knows anything?

07:43.810 --> 07:46.160
What, you're gonna expose him?

07:46.160 --> 07:49.190
It's his own fault for making it sound 
like he's hiding something important.

07:50.250 --> 07:51.750
Good, good.

07:51.750 --> 07:53.470
Get upset about it.

07:53.470 --> 07:55.250
That's when you're at your best.

07:57.830 --> 08:00.490
I smell flames burning.

08:00.490 --> 08:04.500
No sense in sitting idly 
and fizzling out like peat.

08:12.370 --> 08:14.210
That's quite a few.

08:15.280 --> 08:15.940
Huh?

08:16.500 --> 08:17.580
Chise...

08:18.340 --> 08:19.900
Crap!

08:19.900 --> 08:21.570
I got too focused!

08:26.490 --> 08:28.940
After I collected so many?

08:33.500 --> 08:36.110
I smell mixed blood.

08:38.280 --> 08:39.830
What are you?

08:40.070 --> 08:41.380
Hey, now.

08:41.380 --> 08:44.490
He's wearing a student trainee outfit.

08:44.990 --> 08:47.930
You might be punished if you hurt him.

08:47.930 --> 08:50.960
They won't miss one kid.

08:50.960 --> 08:53.310
Wh-Who are you people?!

08:53.310 --> 08:56.130
You're a student here. You ought to know.

08:56.530 --> 08:58.370
We're buddies.

08:58.370 --> 09:00.970
You're sorcerers?

09:02.500 --> 09:04.990
What kind of demi-human are you, though?

09:05.270 --> 09:08.240
Something sandy, something watery...

09:11.800 --> 09:12.970
<i>I can do it.</i>

09:13.400 --> 09:14.430
<i>I can do it.</i>

09:15.090 --> 09:16.610
<i>I did it last time.</i>

09:17.030 --> 09:18.250
<i>I have to do it!</i>

09:23.060 --> 09:25.580
Stay frozen forever!

09:28.680 --> 09:30.460
Gorgon!

09:32.850 --> 09:33.830
Chise...

09:37.420 --> 09:39.720
Weren't you told to stay here?

09:39.720 --> 09:42.220
At least get permission before you leave.

09:43.700 --> 09:47.940
I'm the one who's gonna be miserable 
if something happens to them.

09:48.500 --> 09:49.520
Don't you get it?!

09:49.750 --> 09:51.730
The administrators are on it.

09:51.730 --> 09:53.240
There is no problem.

09:53.240 --> 09:54.400
Stop it.

09:54.780 --> 09:56.860
The way you talk creeps me out.

09:57.970 --> 10:02.610
What is it about me that upsets you, Lucy?

10:04.480 --> 10:06.800
Just leave me alone.

10:07.280 --> 10:10.130
You already left me once before.

10:10.980 --> 10:13.970
Don't act like you're my parent now.

10:13.970 --> 10:14.900
Lucy!

10:21.140 --> 10:22.450
Zoe?

10:23.530 --> 10:24.830
Zoe!

10:30.600 --> 10:31.710
Sir?

10:32.190 --> 10:33.400
You got me.

10:34.570 --> 10:36.430
You're <i>her</i>, aren't you?

10:36.430 --> 10:40.620
The girl who got bought by a mage 
at the London auction last winter.

10:42.890 --> 10:44.660
The Sleigh Beggy.

10:48.980 --> 10:52.320
You even have all your parts.

10:54.450 --> 10:56.140
Don't touch me!

10:58.010 --> 11:00.600
You aren't our instructor, are you?

11:00.600 --> 11:03.520
I never said I was.

11:04.530 --> 11:07.740
I'm a sorcerer bound to the waste tower.

11:08.280 --> 11:09.840
Bound?

11:11.140 --> 11:14.690
I never would have thought 
I'd find a Sleigh Beggy here.

11:17.150 --> 11:18.570
I want you.

11:25.050 --> 11:30.130
I know way more about those 
kinds of tricks than you do.

11:34.510 --> 11:37.210
So there's another inside you!

11:38.020 --> 11:41.620
A rather old one at that, too.

11:41.930 --> 11:45.600
You don't need to be that 
freak's disciple, do you?

11:45.980 --> 11:47.970
You could go on by yourself.

11:48.630 --> 11:49.650
Or...

11:50.470 --> 11:52.720
You could let me take you.

11:53.600 --> 11:56.730
I'd treat you way gentler 
than that <i>thing</i> ever could.

11:57.810 --> 12:00.810
He doesn't even know how valuable you are—

12:00.810 --> 12:01.930
That man...

12:03.090 --> 12:07.370
That man treated me like a person.

12:09.450 --> 12:12.920
So I'd never become yours.

12:13.890 --> 12:15.670
Nor do I need you.

12:18.060 --> 12:20.550
That's some romantic talk.

12:21.750 --> 12:23.000
Oh, well.

12:23.400 --> 12:27.590
They do say you don't want to 
mess with a monster's treasures.

12:28.560 --> 12:32.680
Then again, you may be just 
as much a monster yourself.

12:33.480 --> 12:37.610
That makes for quite a few monsters here.

12:37.940 --> 12:39.150
What are you talking about?

12:39.810 --> 12:42.060
You see that, don't you?

12:43.060 --> 12:46.440
Which means you've killed 
someone, haven't you?

12:51.860 --> 12:53.490
Chise!

12:53.490 --> 12:54.290
Where are you?!

12:55.690 --> 12:56.680
Zoe.

12:57.480 --> 12:59.460
Our time's about up.

12:59.760 --> 13:02.620
You're always welcome to 
participate if you feel like it.

13:06.000 --> 13:08.640
Adolf's on break...

13:13.510 --> 13:14.640
Sorry.

13:14.640 --> 13:15.380
Huh?

13:17.680 --> 13:18.960
You're...

13:18.960 --> 13:21.440
Chise's roommate, aren't you?

13:21.440 --> 13:23.120
Did I hurt you?

13:23.120 --> 13:23.970
No...

13:23.970 --> 13:25.060
Err...

13:25.060 --> 13:26.810
Is something wrong?

13:31.590 --> 13:33.250
Here, you can have this.

13:33.250 --> 13:34.870
I know the feeling.

13:42.630 --> 13:43.560
Chise!

13:44.350 --> 13:46.690
Are you all okay?

13:46.690 --> 13:47.600
Huh?

13:48.350 --> 13:50.060
Uh, and you're...

13:50.280 --> 13:52.650
I'm the actual supervisor.

13:52.650 --> 13:54.920
Who let you in?

13:56.230 --> 13:57.740
Zaccheroni!

13:58.370 --> 14:01.740
You're in charge, but you 
weren't here. What was I to do?

14:01.740 --> 14:04.760
These students haven't 
even signed a waiver!

14:04.760 --> 14:05.460
Here.

14:09.010 --> 14:12.000
I've got plenty of the materials 
you've been looking for, too.

14:12.870 --> 14:15.810
I'm reporting this to our superiors.

14:15.810 --> 14:16.910
Go right ahead.

14:18.000 --> 14:23.000
I think there's someone else 
you need to be more worried about.

14:23.000 --> 14:24.930
In the College, I mean.

14:31.390 --> 14:32.390
Lucy!

14:36.430 --> 14:37.430
Lucy...

15:08.710 --> 15:12.010
You're right, Lucy. I'm a loser.

15:12.840 --> 15:16.000
I'm a failure. I'm not cut out 
to take over the business.

15:17.020 --> 15:22.250
So I thought I was finally free 
when they told me to leave.

15:23.990 --> 15:28.440
That you'd be fine without me, 
because everyone loved you.

15:29.740 --> 15:30.650
I'm sorry.

15:33.380 --> 15:37.270
I'm the one who needs to apologize.

15:38.470 --> 15:42.340
I kept telling myself I had to hate you.

15:43.510 --> 15:48.110
That if you hated the family and me 
along with it, I had no choice.

15:48.930 --> 15:53.810
I knew everyone was treating you coldly.

15:54.490 --> 16:01.320
There was so much for me to learn, 
I wasn't thinking about you at all.

16:01.670 --> 16:09.530
And when you left, there was no 
one who saw me for who I was.

16:09.890 --> 16:11.310
I despised everyone.

16:13.200 --> 16:19.130
But everyone took pride in what they
were making and caring for the spiders.

16:19.130 --> 16:21.840
The spiders weren't guilty
 of anything, either.

16:24.150 --> 16:27.470
It isn't right that they were 
murdered the way they were.

16:27.870 --> 16:31.580
It isn't right that they were ripped 
apart and torn to shreds.

16:32.680 --> 16:35.540
I'm going to find who was behind it!

16:36.100 --> 16:39.000
I'm going to study, master 
sorcery, and become powerful!

16:39.310 --> 16:42.010
Even if I have to use my name as bait!

16:42.300 --> 16:43.420
Lucy!

16:43.830 --> 16:45.380
You can't stop me.

16:47.780 --> 16:53.030
I couldn't come to hate our family enough 
to forget what I saw and move on.

16:55.400 --> 16:59.040
<i>Lucy and I grew up in different environments 
and having seen different things.</i>

16:59.550 --> 17:02.380
<i>There's no changing that fact.</i>

17:06.570 --> 17:10.730
I can't hold onto my anger 
the same way you can.

17:11.390 --> 17:16.050
But Lucy, I always worry for you.

17:16.700 --> 17:18.330
Believe me on that, if nothing else.

17:19.670 --> 17:21.300
I know that.

17:27.260 --> 17:28.830
We're back!

17:30.840 --> 17:32.320
It's the principal.

17:32.760 --> 17:34.330
Hello.

17:34.330 --> 17:35.550
Hello.

17:35.550 --> 17:37.310
I'm glad to see you're all well.

17:37.640 --> 17:38.780
Elias.

17:38.780 --> 17:40.320
Why are you here?

17:40.320 --> 17:44.120
I was asked to help with 
what she's about to do.

17:45.250 --> 17:46.470
Sergeant.

17:46.730 --> 17:48.140
I'm glad to see you here.

17:48.140 --> 17:50.980
There's something I'd like to ask you.

17:54.210 --> 17:59.260
<i>That won't be necessary, Principal Quillyn.</i>

17:59.260 --> 18:00.720
Grandmother?

18:02.050 --> 18:06.390
You must be the Sergeant family 
head, Lizbeth Sergeant.

18:06.390 --> 18:08.110
Your reputation precedes you.

18:08.400 --> 18:13.100
You must not be well, 
to come as your servant bird.

18:13.600 --> 18:18.810
<i>For such an important figure such as 
yourself to have a stroll here...</i>

18:18.810 --> 18:22.160
<i>You must be quite adept at 
making time for yourself.</i>

18:22.160 --> 18:23.450
<i>I'm jealous.</i>

18:23.450 --> 18:27.900
They do say you'll become stiff 
if you sit at your desk all day.

18:28.290 --> 18:33.510
Besides, I have the pleasure of being 
able to speak to each of the students.

18:33.510 --> 18:37.480
I'm glad you enjoy your work.

18:38.010 --> 18:42.850
I haven't had such 
opportunities in my old age.

18:43.350 --> 18:48.910
<i>A letter would never do, so I wished 
to speak with you directly.</i>

18:50.170 --> 18:52.640
About Philomela's withdrawal.

18:53.900 --> 18:56.540
You'd best be off, everyone.

18:56.540 --> 18:58.900
It's time for afternoon tea.

18:58.900 --> 19:00.780
Principal, what is...

19:00.780 --> 19:02.810
<i>You stay, Philomela.</i>

19:04.020 --> 19:05.330
No.

19:05.330 --> 19:08.540
If the withdrawal is due to 
the family's circumstances,

19:08.540 --> 19:12.090
it's for the College and 
the family to discuss.

19:12.510 --> 19:16.560
So long as she has the desire 
to continue her studies.

19:17.390 --> 19:18.640
The desire...

19:19.520 --> 19:22.310
<i>She has no such thing.</i>

19:22.630 --> 19:27.190
<i>She's a failure who can't even 
perform her duties, after all.</i>

19:29.010 --> 19:30.300
What the hell?!

19:37.170 --> 19:37.870
Isaac!

19:41.150 --> 19:41.940
Why...

19:46.760 --> 19:49.020
Elias, I'll see you later.

19:49.880 --> 19:50.770
Sure.

19:55.120 --> 19:56.730
My apologies.

19:56.730 --> 19:58.510
He seems to be quite the youthful one.

19:59.020 --> 20:02.880
You have a rather traditional 
way of thinking.

20:03.280 --> 20:04.630
However...

20:06.390 --> 20:07.490
Indeed.

20:07.490 --> 20:09.500
How very, very irritating.

20:09.500 --> 20:11.030
I don't understand.

20:11.030 --> 20:12.270
It doesn't make sense.

20:12.270 --> 20:13.910
Tell her, Liza.

20:13.910 --> 20:15.510
Bite her!

20:15.990 --> 20:17.980
The College's protectors?

20:17.980 --> 20:19.780
Oh, you know of them?

20:21.830 --> 20:24.790
By the way, I shall have to inform you...

20:25.820 --> 20:28.840
The College will hereby be sealed.

20:28.840 --> 20:30.140
<i>Sealed?</i>

20:30.140 --> 20:31.410
<i>What do you mean by this?</i>

20:31.410 --> 20:33.530
Fly, fly, bird.

20:34.100 --> 20:36.300
Winged, winged rodent.

20:36.660 --> 20:39.850
I'll chase you. I'll catch you. 
I'll tear you apart.

20:39.850 --> 20:46.520
We've had a string of incidents where students 
were harmed in the College's vicinity.

20:46.520 --> 20:50.180
We'll be closing it off for a while 
as a security measure.

20:50.500 --> 20:52.510
<i>I haven't heard such news—</i>

20:52.510 --> 20:54.360
It's an urgent matter.

20:54.360 --> 20:57.390
Guardians will be officially 
informed at a later date.

20:57.810 --> 21:00.660
My fangs are sharp.

21:00.660 --> 21:03.180
My ears are big.

21:03.400 --> 21:06.050
My whiskers quiver.

21:06.350 --> 21:09.120
My eyes watch.

21:09.520 --> 21:12.110
I know you're there.

21:12.110 --> 21:14.490
I can hear you there.

21:14.960 --> 21:17.350
I can see you there.

21:17.930 --> 21:20.420
I'll chase you. I'll catch 
you. I'll tear you apart.

21:20.420 --> 21:22.170
With that, farewell.

21:24.940 --> 21:28.050
That was too early, you three.

21:28.050 --> 21:30.540
She was just so infuriating.

21:30.540 --> 21:31.310
She was!

21:31.730 --> 21:33.010
I see.

21:33.010 --> 21:35.220
They're cat-sìths.

21:35.650 --> 21:38.830
I've never heard of them following 
people's orders, though.

21:38.830 --> 21:41.450
They aren't following orders.

21:41.450 --> 21:43.530
We're equals.

21:44.700 --> 21:49.540
Now, do you see any
 inadequacies in their magic?

21:49.540 --> 21:51.010
Not really.

21:51.010 --> 21:53.300
I wouldn't have needed to get involved.

21:55.570 --> 21:56.730
Ah.

21:56.730 --> 21:59.540
I thought I'd severed her magic power.

22:00.010 --> 22:02.990
You aren't a mere puppet, are you?

22:03.510 --> 22:07.160
I'm Lady Philomela's...

22:12.770 --> 22:17.320
So, it's true that the new 
principal is uncivilized.

22:18.770 --> 22:20.440
Very well.

22:21.370 --> 22:25.950
Just as I'd hoped, I have some time now.
